# event-mpos — Cursor Project Rules

## What This Project Is
An event-based Mobile POS system for retail beauty events (pop-ups, roadshows, brand activations).
Beauty Advisors (BAs) use an Android device to scan customers, build carts, and print receipts.
A warehouse team uses a web dashboard to pack and fulfill orders in real-time.
Payment happens at an external cashier (Guardian, Watsons, etc.) — this system does not handle payment.

## System Components
- **Android mPOS** — used by Beauty Advisors at events (Sunmi V2 Pro device with built-in 58mm thermal printer + 2D barcode scanner)
- **Backend API** — Spring Boot + PostgreSQL, the single source of truth
- **Web Dashboard** — React + TypeScript, used by warehouse team and admins

## Core Concept: Everything Is Scoped to an Event
An Event is the central domain boundary. Products, stock, promotions, orders, and BA assignments all belong to an event. Never design a feature without considering which event it belongs to.

## Tech Stack

### Android
- Kotlin + Jetpack Compose
- Clean Architecture + MVVM
- Room (local cache/offline)
- Retrofit + OkHttp (networking)
- Hilt (dependency injection)
- WorkManager (background jobs + retry queue)
- Sunmi InnerPrinter SDK (thermal printing via AIDL)
- Sunmi Scanner SDK (barcode/QR via AIDL)
- Coil (image loading)
- EncryptedSharedPreferences (secure token storage)

### Backend
- Spring Boot (Kotlin or Java)
- PostgreSQL
- Spring Security + JWT
- Spring WebSocket + STOMP (real-time order push)
- Spring Batch / Scheduler (ERP and member sync jobs)

### Web Dashboard
- React + TypeScript
- SockJS + STOMP.js (WebSocket client)

## Key Architecture Rules
1. **Backend is the source of truth** — Android uses Room as a local cache, never as the authority
2. **Event snapshot on login** — when BA selects an event, download products + stock + members + promotions to Room in one call
3. **Order submission requires network** — cart can be built offline, but submit needs server confirmation; use WorkManager retry queue
4. **Receipt prints only after server confirms the order** — never print on submission attempt
5. **Stock validation is atomic on the server** — use PostgreSQL SELECT FOR UPDATE; never trust client-side stock checks
6. **Idempotency key on every order submission** — prevent duplicate orders from double taps
7. **PrinterPort abstraction** — wrap all Sunmi printer SDK calls behind an interface so hardware can be swapped later

## Order Lifecycle
NEW → PACKING → READY → COLLECTED

## Order Number Strategy
- `id` — UUID (internal, API only)
- `reference_id` — ORD-YYYYMMDD-EVXX-NNN (for support and reconciliation)
- `order_number` — #042 (daily sequence integer, shown on receipt and used verbally)

## Receipt Format (58mm thermal)
Brand name, event name, order number (#042), customer name, product lines (name + price), discount, total, cashier instruction footer.

